  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To determine the volume of the mixture, we need to calculate the sum $3.4+0.68.$\n\nThere is $1$ decimal place in $3.4$ and $2$ decimal places in $0.68.$\n\nTo add the numbers, they both need to have the same number of decimals. Hence, we rewrite the first number so that it has $2$ decimal places:\n\n$$\n3.4=3.40\n$$\n\nNext, we line up the decimal points:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by adding the two numbers just as we would with whole numbers:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  &  \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the mixture is $4.08$ liters.",
